.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREARC-CHECK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securearc-check
.Nd command-line ARC chain validation tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar message-file
.Op Fl n Ar nameserver
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl b Ar bits
.Op Fl r Ar count
.Op Fl m Ar ms
.Op Fl v
.Ar message-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
validates the Authenticated Received Chain (ARC) of an RFC 5322 message file
and prints the chain validation value
.Pq Dq none , Dq pass , or Dq fail
to standard output.
It calls the same
.Fn parseArcSets
and
.Fn validateChain
functions
.Xr securearc 8
uses, in the same order and with the same treatment of a chain that fails to
parse, so a result from
.Nm
is a statement about the shipped verifier rather than about a separate
implementation written to pass tests.
.Pp
This exists so ARC chain validation can be driven by an external conformance
suite the way
.Xr securedkim-check 8
lets the RFC 6376 suite drive DKIM verification.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f Ar message-file
Message file to validate.
May also be given positionally.
Required.
.It Fl n Ar nameserver
DNS nameserver IP address.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl p Ar port
DNS nameserver port.
Default: 53.
Exposed because a conformance suite typically serves its own zone on a high
port, which cannot bind to port 53 unprivileged.
.It Fl b Ar bits
Minimum RSA key bits accepted on an ARC-Message-Signature or ARC-Seal.
Default: 1024.
Reconciled with the RFC 8301 \[sc]3.2 floor exactly as
.Xr securearc 8
does: a value below 1024 is silently raised, so this flag cannot make
.Nm
accept a chain the shipped daemon would reject.
.It Fl r Ar count
Key records to try at one selector before giving up.
Default: 3.
Values above 8 are clamped to 8.
.It Fl m Ar ms
Wall-clock budget for the whole validation, in milliseconds.
Default: 20000, matching the daemon's
.Cm MaxEvaluationMs .
0 disables the limit.
.It Fl v
Verbose: also print the failure reason and the highest ARC instance examined.
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
A verdict was reached and printed to standard output, including
.Dq fail .
.It 2
The tool could not run: the message file could not be read or parsed, or
memory was exhausted.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
The chain validation value is printed alone on a line:
.Dq none
(no ARC sets present),
.Dq pass ,
.Dq fail ,
or
.Dq temperror
(a transient DNS failure or the
.Fl m
deadline was exceeded while validating).
With
.Fl v ,
a
.Dq reason=
field naming the failure and an
.Dq i=
field giving the highest ARC instance examined follow on the same line.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Validate a message using the default resolver:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securearc-check message.eml
.Ed
.Pp
Validate against a conformance suite's own zone, with the failure reason:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securearc-check -n 127.0.0.1 -p 5353 -v message.eml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securearc 8 ,
.Xr securearc-seal 8 ,
.Xr securearc-testkey 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Authenticated Received Chain (ARC) Protocol
.%R RFC 8617
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
